            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h1 id=\"where-the-score-comes-from-fertility-intuition\">Where the score comes from &mdash; fertility intuition</h1>\n<marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||[X = \\frac{T}{D} \\qquad\\qquad \\text{score} = \\frac{1000}{X_{\\max} - X_{\\min}}||]</marimo-tex><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>symbol</th>\n<th>meaning</th>\n<th>can we change it?</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(D||)</marimo-tex></td>\n<td><strong>faithful units</strong> in the text (letter/number runs + each punct char)</td>\n<td><strong>No</strong> &mdash; fixed by the raw text</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(T||)</marimo-tex></td>\n<td><strong>tokens</strong> our tokenizer emits for that text</td>\n<td><strong>Yes</strong> &mdash; this is our only lever</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(X||)</marimo-tex></td>\n<td>fertility = tokens per unit, per language</td>\n<td>falls when <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(T||)</marimo-tex> falls</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">The score rewards the four languages having <strong>equal</strong> fertility (small spread),\nand the assignment requires <strong>every</strong> <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(X \\le 1.2||)</marimo-tex>. Since <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(D||)</marimo-tex> is frozen, the whole\ngame is: <strong>emit fewer tokens for the same text.</strong></span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
