    {
      "id": "Hstk",
      "code_hash": "170be533a5a56aa865be3062e6511f17",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"2-the-unlock-one-token-spanning-many-units\">2&nbsp;&middot;&nbsp;The unlock: one token spanning many units</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">The metric counts <strong>units</strong>, but a <strong>token</strong> can cover as many units as we like.\nIf a single vocab entry <em>is</em> the string <code>\"the government of the union\"</code>, then 6 units\ncollapse into <strong>1 token</strong>:</span>\n<div class=\"language-splus codehilite\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"s\">&quot;the government of the union.&quot;</span>\n<span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"n\">the</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">government</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">of</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">the</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">union</span><span class=\"p\">][</span><span class=\"n\">.</span><span class=\"p\">]</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"o\">&lt;-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"m\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">tokens</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kr\">for</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"m\">6</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">units</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">-&gt;</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"m\">2</span><span class=\"o\">/</span><span class=\"m\">6</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"m\">0.33</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Once merges are allowed to <strong>cross word boundaries</strong>, <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(T||)</marimo-tex> drops <em>below</em> the number of\nunits, so <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(X||)</marimo-tex> goes <strong>below 1.0</strong> &mdash; something subword BPE can never do.</span>\n<h3 id=\"where-the-savings-come-from-repetition-not-length\">Where the savings come from: repetition, not length</h3>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>1 vocab slot spent on&hellip;</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: right;\">occurrences</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: right;\">tokens removed</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>\"of the\"</code></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">312&times;</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">+312</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>\"in India\"</code></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">204&times;</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">+204</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>\"Constantinople\"</code></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">3&times;</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">+3</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Think of each of the 10,000 vocab slots as a <strong>coupon</strong>. Spending it on a phrase that\nappears 300 times removes ~300 tokens; on a rare long word, ~3. <strong>Frequency pays, not\nlength</strong> &mdash; and the greedy max-heap already picks highest-frequency pairs first.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
