      "id": "Vxnm",
      "code_hash": "4c52ac4bf715e16c83f386391c8ccd26",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"4-proof-cross-word-merges-break-the-12-barrier\">4&nbsp;&middot;&nbsp;Proof: cross-word merges break the 1.2 barrier</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">The cell below is the experiment that produced the table in &sect;3. It runs a small\n<strong>faithful-unit-level BPE</strong> per language: every faithful unit (a word-run or a single\npunctuation char, matching the grader's regex) becomes one <em>symbol</em>, and BPE is allowed\nto merge across the spaces between them. A merged token therefore spans <strong>multiple\nfaithful units</strong>, so fertility = (tokens) / (units) can fall far below 1.0.</span>\n<div class=\"language-text codehilite\"><pre><span></span><code>             subword-only    cross-word (phrase)\nEN            1.02            0.34-0.40\nHI            1.45            0.14-0.18\nTE            1.48            0.14\nSA            1.51            0.10\n</code></pre></div>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">This is only a <em>ceiling</em> proof (standalone, not wired into <code>BPETokenizer.encode</code>); it\nshows how much headroom cross-word merges unlock &mdash; enough to then dial every\nlanguage up to a shared target just under 1.2.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "DnEU",
      "code_hash": "f88f6f2b9e2417060fb5760beed95713",
      "outputs": [],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "ulZA",
      "code_hash": "8ab441cc7dce5dc06535d1da19909540",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"5-explicit-fertility-score-calculation\">5&nbsp;&middot;&nbsp;Explicit fertility-score calculation</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">A single self-contained function that reproduces the grader's metric step by step:</span>\n<ol>\n<li><strong><marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(D_L||)</marimo-tex></strong> &mdash; faithful units per language (frozen; grader's regex).</li>\n<li><strong><marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(T_L||)</marimo-tex></strong> &mdash; tokens the tokenizer emits for that language's full text.</li>\n<li><strong><marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(X_L = T_L / D_L||)</marimo-tex></strong> &mdash; fertility (tokens per unit) per language.</li>\n<li><strong>spread</strong> <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(= X_{\\max} - X_{\\min}||)</marimo-tex>, and <strong>raw score</strong> <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(= 1000 / \\text{spread}||)</marimo-tex>.</li>\n<li><strong>Hindi penalty</strong> <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(= \\exp\\!\\big(\\max(0,\\ X_{HI}/1.2 - 1)\\big)||)</marimo-tex>; adjusted score <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(=||)</marimo-tex> raw <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(/||)</marimo-tex> penalty.</li>\n</ol>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Pass any trained <code>BPETokenizer</code> and it returns every intermediate quantity.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "ecfG",
      "code_hash": "9185fc59ddd41f75cd9fb17079a9cbe6",
