          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"6-cross-word-tokenizer-driving-every-x-below-08\">6&nbsp;&middot;&nbsp;Cross-word tokenizer &mdash; driving every <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(X||)</marimo-tex> below 0.8</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\"><code>PhraseBPETokenizer</code> changes exactly <strong>one</strong> thing versus the base tokenizer: it\npretokenizes by <strong>whole lines</strong> instead of by words. BPE merges are then free to cross\nspaces, so a single token can span many faithful units and fertility drops below 1.0.\nTrained on the pooled line corpus at a 10k vocab, <strong>all four <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(X||)</marimo-tex> land well under 0.8.</strong>\nDecoding is unchanged (tokens are still exact byte-symbol strings), so it stays lossless.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
