            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"7-vocab-distribution-by-language-script\">7&nbsp;&middot;&nbsp;Vocab distribution by language / script</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Every vocab entry is decoded back to text and classified by script. This shows how the\n10k shared slots are split across languages &mdash; and how many are genuine <strong>cross-word</strong>\ntokens (contain a space, i.e. span multiple faithful units). Latin still dominates because\nEnglish's 1-byte alphabet and large pretoken count win the greedy heap; Devanagari serves\nboth Hindi and Sanskrit.</span></span>"
